   {
    "title": "Gigapet Nutrition Log",
    "description": "Using NodeJS with Express framework, developed a back-end for a nutritional log app that allows users to keep track of a family's diet choices. \n\nThe project was completed in 1 week's time with 3 other web development students, who created a ReactJS app to work with the Node server I constructed.\n\n• The app uses a calendar component to make dynamic queries to the back-end to receive data across a range of dates.\n• The server uses JSON web tokens for authentication and authorization, and SQLite for database management.\n• The server uses SQLite for database management to take advantage of the system's compact library, configuration-free usage, and compatibility with free tools like SQLite studio.\n\nTest Account : Login: homer | Password: simpson \nCheck the month of March 2019 for seeded data.",
    "dateRange": {},
